The program reads three lines: a principal amount, a yearly interest rate in percent and a number of years. It computes simple interest as principal × rate × years / 100, rounded to 2 decimals, and adds it to the principal. It prints the interest and the total without leading spaces. Inputs are truncated to the precision of their COBOL fields (2 decimals for amounts and rates, whole years).

